---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { brand } from "@/lib/brand";

export const prerender = true;

const canonical = `${brand.siteUrl}/guides/send-large-files-without-filling-computer`;

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "TechArticle",
  headline: "How to Send Large Files Without Filling Up Your Hard Drive",
  description: "Learn how to transfer 20GB–500GB files directly without cloud storage desktop apps consuming your SSD disk space with local cache files.",
  url: canonical,
  author: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: brand.productName,
  },
  publisher: {
    "@type": "Organization",
    name: brand.productName,
    url: brand.siteUrl,
  },
  datePublished: "2026-05-01",
  dateModified: "2026-10-04",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`How to Send Large Files Without Filling Up Your Hard Drive | ${brand.productName}`}
  description="Stop cloud sync apps from cloning 200GB project folders onto your local SSD. How direct browser streaming transfers large files with zero disk caching."
  canonical={canonical}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleSchema)} />
  </Fragment>

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-slate-50 text-slate-950">
    <header class="border-b border-slate-200 bg-white">
      <nav class="mx-auto flex max-w-7xl items-center justify-between px-4 py-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">
          <span class="flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-blue-600 text-white">↑</span>
          {brand.productName}
        </a>
        <div class="hidden items-center gap-6 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 sm:flex">
          <a class="hover:text-blue-700" href="/transfer">Transfer</a>
          <a class="hover:text-blue-700" href="/plans">Plans</a>
          <a class="hover:text-blue-700" href="/directory">Directory</a>
          <a class="hover:text-blue-700" href="/guides">Guides</a>
          <a class="hover:text-blue-700" href="/tools/transfer-speed-calculator">Calculator</a>
        </div>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <article class="bg-white py-16 sm:py-20 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-blue-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-700">
          <span>Local Storage Optimization</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-5xl">
          How to Send Large Files Without Filling Up Your Hard Drive
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
          Ever dropped a 100GB video project into Dropbox or Google Drive to share with a client, only to receive a macOS warning: "Your startup disk is almost full"? Here is why cloud sync apps devour local storage and how to send files with zero local disk overhead.
        </p>

        <div class="prose prose-slate mt-8 max-w-none space-y-6 text-slate-800 leading-relaxed">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-950">The Hidden Cache Problem of Cloud Sync Apps</h2>
          <p>
            Traditional sync clients (Google Drive Desktop, Dropbox, Microsoft OneDrive) work by maintaining a mirrored folder on your local file system. Even when you designate a folder as "Online-Only", uploading a 50GB file requires the sync client to copy that 50GB into a hidden local cache directory (<code>~/Library/CloudStorage/...</code>) while it uploads.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you only have 30GB of free space on your MacBook or Windows laptop, the upload will crash and lock up your operating system.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-950">The Zero-Cache In-Browser Transfer Alternative</h2>
          <p>
            Gigasend bypasses your local file system entirely. Using the HTML5 File System API and Web Streams:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3 text-slate-700">
            <li>Your browser reads the file chunks directly from your external drive, camera card, or local SSD into memory buffers.</li>
            <li>No duplicate copies or hidden cache files are written to your computer.</li>
            <li>Once transmitted to the edge, the buffer is immediately released by JavaScript garbage collection.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-12 rounded-2xl bg-blue-600 p-8 text-white text-center">
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold">Transfer Large Files Without Wasting Disk Space</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 text-blue-100 text-sm">
            Drag and drop directly from external drives. Free up to 10GB with zero local cache footprint.
          </p>
          <a
            href="/transfer"
            class="mt-6 inline-block rounded-lg bg-white px-8 py-3 text-base font-bold text-blue-600 shadow-md hover:bg-slate-50"
          >
            Send File Directly Now
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
